{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"t":"Reading","w":0.079668324788411571,"x":0.79146887209594519,"h":0.017131283089465987,"y":0.097249598834963313,"c":1},{"x":0.088477373056560768,"t":"The Banda Islands were ruled by local sultans who insisted on maintaining a neutral trading","c":1,"y":0.14244186031912909,"w":0.73251027425130211,"h":0.015988372380376759},{"y":0.15988372079761526,"t":"policy towards foreign powers. This allowed them to avoid the presence of Portuguese or Spanish","x":0.086419753299206453,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"w":0.77572016398111976},{"t":"troops on their soil, but it also left them unprotected from other invaders. In 1621, the Dutch","h":0.019458413545318742,"y":0.17412798849369115,"x":0.086345228626230147,"w":0.73677469889322911,"c":1},{"w":0.77366256713867188,"h":0.017503492402524912,"y":0.1918604649570772,"c":1,"t":"arrived and took over. Once securely in control of the Bandas, the Dutch went to work protecting","x":0.086419745134367745},{"w":0.76352656046549483,"h":0.019368743447167769,"t":"their new investment. They concentrated all nutmeg production into a few easily guarded areas,","y":0.20740845496703586,"x":0.086352611979691948,"c":1},{"h":0.019681503691296953,"t":"uprooting and destroying any trees outside the plantation zones. Anyone caught growing a nutmeg","x":0.086347097377703602,"y":0.22476061408244985,"w":0.78409754435221346,"c":1},{"t":"seedling or carrying seeds without the proper authority was severely punished. In addition,","x":0.086362212752090009,"y":0.24118798396576291,"h":0.019009202613426313,"c":1,"w":0.72646565755208337},{"y":0.2601744184852125,"c":1,"t":"all exported nutmeg was covered with lime to make sure there was no chance a fertile seed","x":0.088477357676344279,"w":0.72222223917643236,"h":0.01308824372937456},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"which could be grown elsewhere would leave the islands. There was only one obstacle to Dutch","w":0.7633744812011718,"y":0.27616279055105852,"c":1,"x":0.086419755149156854},{"c":1,"t":"domination. One of the Banda Islands, a sliver of land called Run, only 3 km long by less than","x":0.086364513779216071,"y":0.29198666160302023,"h":0.018602738532076613,"w":0.75114201863606778},{"y":0.3094817431335235,"w":0.76543207804361979,"h":0.016195524146054074,"c":1,"t":"1 km wide, was under the control of the British. After decades of fighting for control of this tiny","x":0.086419763334370805},{"t":"island, the Dutch and British arrived at a compromise settlement, the Treaty of Breda, in 1667.","y":0.32412790713239814,"w":0.75720163981119792,"x":0.086419763890697165,"h":0.018922740635237245,"c":1},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"t":"Intent on securing their hold over every nutmeg-producing island, the Dutch offered a trade: if the","x":0.086419744191084266,"y":0.34302325566812764,"w":0.77983540852864586},{"w":0.77983540852864586,"h":0.016029460129664774,"y":0.36042402838392074,"c":1,"t":"British would give them the island of Run, they would in turn give Britain a distant and much less","x":0.088477357357537201},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"w":0.77160491943359377,"t":"valuable island in North America. The British agreed. That other island was Manhattan, which is","c":1,"x":0.086419762399579741,"y":0.37632508816711896},{"t":"how New Amsterdam became New York. The Dutch now had a monopoly over the nutmeg trade","x":0.086419754238012375,"w":0.76954732259114567,"c":1,"h":0.015998644317698818,"y":0.39389534869136611},{"c":1,"t":"which would last for another century.","x":0.086209987954825262,"w":0.30087994893391928,"y":0.40880240944587509,"h":0.017239090972289262},{"y":0.44316843320067889,"w":0.75102879842122394,"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"Then, in 1770, a Frenchman named Pierre Poivre successfully smuggled nutmeg plants to safety","x":0.086419757061893185,"c":1},{"t":"in Mauritius, an island off the coast of Africa. Some of these were later exported to the Caribbean","h":0.017354366495696327,"y":0.45928150193312423,"c":1,"w":0.75937021891276046,"x":0.086355687993525027},{"w":0.75319630940755211,"x":0.08637073680142407,"y":0.47495838443219596,"h":0.019103561329476548,"c":1,"t":"where they thrived, especially on the island of Grenada. Next, in 1778, a volcanic eruption in the"},{"x":0.088477368349753269,"w":0.76337448120117191,"y":0.49411071845099874,"c":1,"t":"Banda region caused a tsunami that wiped out half the nutmeg groves. Finally, in 1809, the British","h":0.016195524146054185},{"w":0.72222223917643236,"y":0.51017441845843658,"h":0.016032884483202614,"x":0.086419744512966093,"t":"returned to Indonesia and seized the Banda Islands by force. They returned the islands to the","c":1},{"t":"Dutch in 1817, but not before transplanting hundreds of nutmeg seedlings to plantations in several","h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"x":0.086419746076268303,"y":0.52761627892393592,"w":0.76748972574869778},{"w":0.5558802795410156,"t":"locations across southern Asia. The Dutch nutmeg monopoly was over.","h":0.018499798993761085,"x":0.086250668316710202,"y":0.54216402209192205,"c":1},{"w":0.71193415323893228,"y":0.57703488357493626,"t":"Today, nutmeg is grown in Indonesia, the Caribbean, India, Malaysia, Papua New Guinea and","x":0.086419754553671554,"h":0.016015764400450716,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.59302325565442005,"h":0.017441860778592888,"t":"Sri Lanka, and world nutmeg production is estimated to average between 10,000 and 12,000 tonnes","x":0.086419756105401382,"w":0.75720163981119792},{"h":0.013200611613243263,"y":0.61331248487043788,"w":0.07000332514444986,"c":1,"t":"per year.","x":0.086397514279697038},{"h":0.011627907185728592,"x":0.84567901243948618,"c":1,"t":"17","y":0.91860465100544442,"w":0.024691357612609877}]}